# The far end of the harbour pier: the lighthouse, and Cray's cutter, unloading kelp.
room pier_end "The Pier End"
  bg bg_pierend_wide
  width 2560
  music music_sea
  grade "brightness(0.95) saturate(0.85)"
  ambience sea
  perspective horizon 455 ref 875 height 330
  walk (545,875) (560,790) (760,770) (1010,705) (1230,672) (1420,640) (1800,600) (1560,760) (1300,875)
  entry 640,830

  # Wilf, loading the hand cart; Bartle, by the lamp, whose turn it supposedly is.
  sprite npc_weather_body at 885,765 size 1 idle speaker weather for wilf grade "saturate(0.6) brightness(0.72)" if not inquiry_done
  sprite npc_weather_body at 1330,662 size 1 flip idle speaker weather2 for bartle grade "saturate(0.6) brightness(0.72)" if not inquiry_done
  # Vane, ashore once the flag's down, by the lamp, looking at the crates she carried.
  sprite npc_vane_body at 1330,662 size 1 flip idle speaker vane for vane grade "saturate(0.75) brightness(0.88)"

  hotspot town "back along the pier"
    area 0,360 520x120
    stand 600,840
    exit dock
    look "Back along the pier, the lights of Port Vela, and somewhere among them the Salty Keel, singing."

  hotspot cutter "Cray's cutter"
    area (540,290) (900,300) (1010,480) (990,600) (780,640) (420,600) (400,520)
    stand 830,770
    look "A grey cutter with a cloud on her furled sail: the one that ran out of the lagoon ahead of us. Fast, neat, and built for getting home first, which is the whole of Cray's business."
    open "There's nothing aboard but the smell of kelp and the feeling of being watched by a gangplank."
    talk "I say something cutting to the cutter. It's the best I can do at this hour."

  hotspot wilf "Weather man"
    show if not inquiry_done
    area 830,540 110x225
    stand 1010,760
    look "One of Cray's men, grey coat, yellow armband, carrying a crate of kelp to the cart as if it were a sleeping child. He is very polite and very large."
    talk "He sets the crate down on the cart and touches his hat."
      talk weather4
    give "“Can't take anything without a docket, sir. Mr Cray's very strict.”"

  hotspot bartle "Weather man"
    show if not inquiry_done
    area 1285,465 100x195
    stand 1250,700
    look "Another of Cray's men, by the lamp, holding a crate and a grudge. The grudge is about whose turn it is."
    talk "He nods at his colleague. “Talk to Wilf, sir. Wilf's on menacing.”"
      talk weather4
    give "“Docket first, sir.”"

  hotspot vane "Captain Vane"
    show if quarantine_lifted
    area 1280,440 105x225
    stand 1180,700
    look "Captain Vane, ashore, by the lamp, with her hands behind her back, inspecting Cray's kelp crates the way she'd inspect a crew she was about to flog."
    talk "She doesn't turn round. “Clerk.”"
      talk vane4
    give "“Keep it, clerk. I've carried enough of other people's cargo.”"

  hotspot crates "kelp crates"
    area 940,530 270x150
    stand 1180,700
    look "Crates stencilled QUARANTINE STN, G.K., with a little cloud painted over the stencil, badly, which is how you know the stencil mattered."
    open "Nailed shut, and two large men are standing next to them, being polite in my direction."
    state if kelp_seen
      look "The same crates as on the Marrow's deck: QUARANTINE STN, G.K., with a cloud painted over it. I've seen what's inside. It burns like a lie."

  hotspot kelp_manifest "manifest on the crate"
    show if not has kelp_manifest and not kelp_proof
    area 990,525 150x45
    stand 1180,700
    item kelp_manifest
    look "A manifest, tacked to the top crate for whoever signs for it. Nobody's signing for it. They're too busy deciding whose turn it is to be menacing."
    pickup "While they argue about whose turn it is to be menacing, I lift the manifest off the crate. I'm customs. Manifests come to me the way cats come to people who don't want cats."
      set kelp_proof

  hotspot stack "stacked crates"
    area 170,590 370x240
    nowalk
    look "More of Cray's kelp, stacked for the cart, sacked and stencilled. Enough fog for a month of Tuesdays."

  hotspot lighthouse "the lighthouse"
    area 2110,90 170x450
    nowalk
    look "The Vela light, turning over the harbour mouth. Three years I watched ships leave by it. Tonight I came home by it. It looks smaller from the sea, which I'm told is the point."

  hotspot sea "the harbour mouth"
    area 1900,560 660x320
    nowalk
    look "The harbour mouth, black and moving, and past it the Straits. They don't look any different. I am, I think."

  use crowbar on crates if kelp_seen
    "I've already seen inside one of these, on the Marrow. Once was plenty. Kelp smells exactly like a lie on fire."
  use crowbar on crates
    "One of the Weather men clears his throat, politely, and shifts a crate to his other arm, so his hand is free. I put the crowbar away."
  use stamp on wilf
    "“Customs, Wilf,” says one. “Told you,” says the other. Neither of them stops unloading."
  use kelp_manifest on wilf
    "“You keep that, sir. It's only kelp.” He thinks about it. “Don't keep it too hard.”"
